From bd893ac96bfc63fdcabc8e7fce23b739bc8b2364 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:05:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): record all thread stacks when the event loop
 stalls

The gateway can stop answering for seconds with no trace of why. A
watchdog thread now pings the asyncio loop every second; when a ping is
not serviced within logging.stall_watchdog_threshold_seconds (5), it
writes logs/stalls/stall-<UTC time>.txt: every thread's stack (file, line
and function only, no locals or arguments), the coroutine chain of the
task the loop is running, the live child processes by command name and
the requests in flight per method, and later the length of the stall.
One report per 60 s, the newest 50 kept. SIGUSR2 dumps all stacks to
logs/stalls/sigusr2.txt. logging.stall_watchdog: false turns it off.
